  <constraints>
    <constraint source="ADR-003 / spec NFR-01">Scope: every read guard added here. Fail CLOSED: an unreadable contact state, an unreadable root state, or a missing row is treated as INACTIVE. The root state rides the existing flag read and its `Unreadable` value; do not add a read path that can fail open.</constraint>
    <constraint source="C5 fix direction">Scope: inactive contact. Applies to every contact-sourced term on both planes (direct grants, organization grants, and — while they still exist on the workforce plane — the standing and organization-expansion terms) and to a systemuser's linked contact. The check is LIVE per composition (not inside the 60-second grant cache or the 10-minute identity cache); prefer riding an existing live contact read over adding a round trip (NFR-02). `SubjectStandingGrantReader.ReadForContactAsync` (`SubjectStandingGrantReader.cs:130-138`) reads the contact row live today, but it serves the standing term, which task 142 escalation (d) may retire, and CIAM never calls it — so the guard must not depend on that reader surviving: if it is the carrier, a test pins that removing the standing term does not remove the contact-state check. A systemuser's own membership term is unaffected.</constraint>
    <constraint source="ADR-028 A1 / no-hijack">Scope: contact resolution at sign-in. Owned and implemented by task 141 (an oid that matches an INACTIVE contact denies with its own reason code and never falls through to the email fallback, the oid bind or contact creation; an inactive contact is never an email-bind target). THIS task VERIFIES it on both planes with the tests named in acceptance and does not add a second implementation. If 141's rule is missing or incomplete on either plane, STOP and amend 141 (escalation) — do not patch resolution here.</constraint>
    <constraint source="C5 fix direction">Scope: inactive root. `statecode` joins the existing batched root-flag read; an inactive (or unreadable) root is removed from every contact-sourced contribution in `ApplyVetoPipeline`, mirroring the Restricted slot's survivor rule, so a systemuser's own membership survives exactly as it does on Restricted. Reactivating the root restores access with no data change (this is why the guard is read-time, not a grant deactivation).</constraint>
    <constraint source="C5 fix direction / ADR-009">Scope: invalidation. ONE invalidation routine (extend `ExternalParticipationService.InvalidateAsync`, CLAUDE.md §11) called by every grant-write path found by grepping `RemoveAsync(` with `ExternalAccessResource` — at least grant, invite-and-grant, revoke, close-project and set-record-share-expiry, plus task 140's contact-side grant route and task 142's materializer if either has landed. It removes every key under which the contact's grant set can be cached: either remove under EVERY tenant id a grant set can be cached under — the request tenant, the configured `Ciam:TenantId`, and every configured customer workforce tenant (task 141 introduces that setting; in Model 1 it can differ from `AzureAd:TenantId`) — or change the grant cache to one deployment-constant tenant component so every plane shares one entry (defensible under D-13, one BFF per customer). If you choose the second, the ADR-009 / ITenantCache tenant-scoping contract is in play: record it as a CLAUDE.md §6.5 path A or B in the task notes and stop for approval before merging. Any key-shape change bumps `CacheVersion` past the value task 131 set (131 moves it 4→5).</constraint>
    <constraint source="C5 fix direction">Scope: organization grants. Granting, revoking, expiring or closing an organization grant invalidates every ACTIVE member's entry, reusing `ExternalOrganizationMembership.QueryActiveMembersAsync`. No silent cap: an organization over `MaxMembersPerSweep` is paged to completion; if paging cannot complete, the member ids not invalidated are logged at warning with the count and the write's response is unaffected (staleness is bounded by the 60-second TTL, and that bound is stated in the log).</constraint>
    <constraint source="owner 2026-09-10">Scope: failure reporting on write endpoints. An invalidation failure is non-fatal and never turns a successful write into an error; a failed REVOKE still returns its existing ProblemDetails message, never a bare 500.</constraint>
    <constraint source="owner round 2">Scope: things this task must not touch. `SpeContainerMembershipService.GrantMembershipAsync` stays at zero callers. Do not change the grant expiry default (+90 days, `ExternalGrantLifecycle.DefaultExpiryDays`). Do not implement the junction date or organization-state guards here — they are task 109's, in the same query; this task verifies them.</constraint>
    <constraint source="D-1 / ADR-036 / ADR-052">Scope: the reconciliation job. No plugins. Any change stays inside the existing `ExternalAccessReconciliationJob` (`IScheduledJob`, registered via `AddScheduledJob`); no new job, no new timer. Enabling the schedule or writes is an OWNER decision (D-2 part 3): this task produces the report-only counts and a recommendation, obtains the decision through the escalation below, and then makes the configuration match it.</constraint>
    <constraint source="owner 2026-09-10 / spec">Scope: verification. No Dataverse test in CI; live checks are a MANUAL gate using existing test users and an existing CIAM test contact in the correct BU; no user relocation.</constraint>
    <constraint source="ADR-038">Scope: tests. KEEP paths; the cache round-trip test uses a real `ITenantCache` over an in-memory `IDistributedCache`; no `Mock&lt;HttpMessageHandler&gt;`, no DI-registration or ctor null-check tests.</constraint>
    <constraint source="CLAUDE.md §10">Scope: this task's PR. Placement decision citing `.claude/constraints/bff-extensions.md`; publish size from fresh master and fresh branch worktrees at SHORT paths, Compress-Archive on both, equal file counts, both sizes and the delta; ≤60 MB; no new HIGH CVE.</constraint>
  </constraints>

