  <steps mode="directional">
    <step order="0">Re-verify every anchor. Confirm tasks 109, 136 and 141 are merged, and whether tasks 131, 132, 138, 140 and 142 have changed `ExternalParticipationService.cs`, `RootRecordFlags` or the grant-write endpoints; rebase your plan onto their shapes.</step>
    <step order="1">Before-state in dev: count and list active grants whose contact is inactive, active grants whose root is inactive, and — by running the reconciliation job in report-only mode — the R1/R2/R3 rows. Record all of it in the task notes. These are access removals.</step>
    <step order="2">Inactive contact: live per-composition contact-state check on both planes and the systemuser linked contact. Verify (do not re-implement) task 141's sign-in denial for an oid bound to an inactive contact on both planes.</step>
    <step order="3">Inactive root: `statecode` in the root-flag read, the flag type extended, the veto applied with the systemuser survivor rule.</step>
    <step order="4">Invalidation: one routine, every grant-write caller switched to it, CIAM-tenant coverage, organization fan-out without a silent cap.</step>
    <step order="5">Verify task 109's guards on BOTH planes (organization inactive, membership end date, membership start date) with a seam test per guard per plane; if any is missing on either plane, fire the escalation rather than re-implementing it here.</step>
    <step order="6">Reconciliation posture: write the recommendation (enable schedule? writes? add rules for inactive contacts or roots, or rely on the read guards?), fire the owner escalation, then make `ExternalAccessModule.cs` / `appsettings.template.json` / `DEPLOY-CHECKLIST.md` match the recorded decision.</step>
    <step order="7">Correct `notes/investigation/04-grant-lifecycle.md:116` (0-second revoke latency). Tests, perturbations, build, suites, publish size, MANUAL live gate, notes at `projects/unified-access-control-r2/notes/task-137-soft-revocation.md`, TASK-INDEX and POML status, `check-task-status-drift.ps1`.</step>
  </steps>

  <escalation>
    <trigger>OWNER DECISION (expected to fire): the reconciliation job's posture — schedule enabled or not, writes enabled or report-only, and whether to add writer rules for inactive contacts and inactive roots. Present the Step 1 counts and this recommendation: keep inactive contacts and roots as READ guards only (reactivation then restores access with no data repair), enable the schedule in report-only first, and enable writes only after the owner has reviewed one report. Do not change the registration or the WritesEnabled key until the owner answers.</trigger>
