  <acceptance-criteria>
    <criterion testable="true">Inactive contact at sign-in (task 141's rule, verified here on BOTH planes): a CIAM token and a workforce token whose oid is bound to an inactive contact each get 403 with 141's inactive reason code; no email lookup, no oid bind and no contact creation occur (asserted), even when an active contact shares the email.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">Inactive contact after sign-in: a CIAM contact and a workforce contact deactivated AFTER their identity was resolved and cached lose every contact-sourced record on the next composition, while the grant cache and the identity cache are both warm (asserted with warm caches).</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">Inactive contact, workforce contact-only: every contact-sourced term contributes nothing on the next composition, independent of the identity cache (test with a warm identity cache).</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">Inactive linked contact of a systemuser: its grants contribute nothing; the systemuser's own membership rights are unchanged.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">An unreadable contact state denies contact-sourced access (fail closed).</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">Inactive root: an active FullAccess grant on an inactive project, matter or work assignment confers nothing to a contact on either plane (one test per root type); a systemuser's membership on the same inactive root survives; reactivating the root (flag double flips back) restores the contact's access with no other change.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">An unreadable root state removes contact-sourced access (existing `Unreadable` semantics extended).</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">Invalidation: after a revoke by a workforce admin, a subsequent CIAM request for the revoked contact reads fresh grants (no stale hit) — proven through a real `ITenantCache` over an in-memory `IDistributedCache` with entries written under both the CIAM and the workforce tenant.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">Invalidation: granting, revoking, expiring and closing an ORGANIZATION grant each invalidates every active member's entry, including an organization with more members than `MaxMembersPerSweep`.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">An invalidation failure never changes the write endpoint's status code or body; a failed revoke still returns its ProblemDetails message.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">Grep shows no remaining private `cache.RemoveAsync(..., ExternalAccessResource, ...)` copy in `Api/ExternalAccess/**`; every grant-write path calls the single routine.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">Tracked parts verified on BOTH planes with named tests (after tasks 109 and 135): an inactive organization's grants and memberships confer nothing; a membership past `sprk_enddate` confers nothing; a membership before `sprk_startdate` confers nothing; the deny veto's organization axis still binds a former member. The notes map #1006 (read half → 109, write half → 117) and #999 (→ 109/110) to their evidence.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">Reconciliation posture: the owner's decision is recorded verbatim in the task notes and in `DEPLOY-CHECKLIST.md`, and the job registration and `ExternalAccess:Reconciliation:WritesEnabled` match it exactly.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">Step 1 before-state (counts plus lists, including the report-only R1/R2/R3 output) is recorded before merge.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">`notes/investigation/04-grant-lifecycle.md:116` no longer claims 0-second revoke latency.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">Perturbation: removing the contact-state check, removing `statecode` from the root-flag read, removing the CIAM-tenant removal, or removing the organization fan-out each turns at least one test red; letting an inactive oid-bound contact fall through to the email path turns the verification test red (proving the test bites on 141's rule). All reverted before completion.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">MANUAL live gate (dev, no CI), with an existing CIAM test contact holding a direct grant and an organization grant on a test matter: deactivate the matter → the external SPA loses it within one request; reactivate → it returns; deactivate the contact → the next sign-in is refused; revoke the organization grant as an existing non-admin Write-holder → the CIAM session loses it on the next request (no 60-second wait). Test records restored afterwards; evidence in the task notes.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">Build green; full BFF unit suite, seam suite and ArchTests green; publish size reported (both sizes, delta, zip tool, file counts) and ≤60 MB; no new HIGH CVE.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">Test scope: cover the stated contract plus the edge cases named above; anything beyond that needs a one-line justification in the task notes.</criterion>
