WHAT CHANGED: (1) inactive contact — ExternalParticipationService.ReadContactStateAsync reads contacts(id)?$select=statecode LIVE (never cached across requests; remembered for one request in HttpContext.Items; a fault is never remembered); only statecode 0 is Active, 404 = Inactive, any other failure or a null state = Unreadable. ComposeContactPlaneAsync (CIAM + workforce contact) composes the EMPTY set for anything but Active, read first; ComposeForSystemUserAsync drops the linked contact's grant term (read only when that term could contribute, NFR-02), keeps the contact as the wall subject, never touches the membership term. (2) inactive root — statecode joins the existing batched flag read (RootFlagColumns); FlagsFrom maps non-zero OR null to RootRecordFlags.IsInactive (fail closed); Unreadable also carries it; ApplyVetoPipeline's Restricted slot keys on RemovesContactSourcedAccess (Restricted OR inactive), same systemuser survivor rule; reactivation restores with no data change. (3) ONE invalidation routine — ExternalParticipationService.InvalidateGrantSetsAsync(contacts, organizations): organizations expand to ACTIVE members (ExternalOrganizationMembership.ActiveMembersFilter, @odata.nextLink followed, 500/page, 200-page backstop, an incomplete walk logged at warning with the count and the 60 s bound), removal under every tenant (request tid, explicit, Ciam:TenantId, AzureAd:TenantId, every WorkforceIdentity:CustomerTenantIds, plus the lower-case D form of any GUID), bounded parallel removals, never throws. /grant + /invite-and-grant (via CreateGrantAsync), /revoke (keyed on the revoked ROW's grantee), /close-project and /set-record-share-expiry all call it; their private RemoveAsync / ExtractTenantId copies and ITenantCache parameters are deleted (grep: no RemoveAsync or ExternalAccessResource left in Api/ExternalAccess). ExternalOrganizationMembership moved unchanged to Infrastructure/ExternalAccess (pure file move). (4) notes/investigation/04-grant-lifecycle